imazen26 K300 production-corpus byte-identity — FIRST RUN EVER.

commit:   0094ec03b
host:     i265 x86_64, 20 threads
date:     2026-09-10
command:  tools/imazen26_gate.sh   (IM26_DIM=512, cli_qp 32)
grid:     20 images x {preset,bd} = 40 cells

RESULT    40 / 40 byte-identical, from BOTH asset sets (see below). 61 s.

WHY THIS IS THE FIRST RUN IN 48 DAYS, AND THE FIRST EVER IN CI. The gate ran
once before, 40/40, in the commit that created it (304c5832c, 2026-07-24). Its
corpus lived at /root/work/imazen26-cache/K300 on `dev-32gb`, a rented fleet
box — imazen26_sweep_2026-07-24.meta records that campaign ending at the
"box-lifetime limit". The corpus was never committed and never copied anywhere
persistent, so from then on `corpus_dir imazen26-cache/K300` resolved to an
absent path and every cell reported MISSING. The gate itself was correct; it
had no input.

CORRECTION to an earlier version of this file, which claimed the gate had never
run anywhere and cited its mode 0644 as proof. Both were wrong. The mode was an
accident at creation — the same campaign added imazen26_sweep.sh as 100755 and
imazen26_gate.sh as 100644 — so it was invoked as `bash tools/...`. File mode is
not evidence about whether a script has ever run.

ASSETS. Published at the R2 prefix imazen26-k300-512/ as the 20 images
CENTRE-CROPPED to 512x512, which is all the gate ever encodes (it feeds
`crop:<png>` at IM26_DIM). Originals 290 MiB, crops 6.1 MiB.

EQUIVALENCE, MEASURED not argued. The gate was run against the 290 MiB
originals and against the 6.1 MiB crops. Both produced 40/40 and the SAME byte
count for every one of the 40 cells (diff of the two cell lists is empty).
examples/crop_png.rs reuses identity_run's own decode (png EXPAND | STRIP_16,
same RGB conversion) and the same centre arithmetic as the `crop:` branch, so
`crop:` on a crop is the identity map — but the check is what makes it a fact.

PROVENANCE GOTCHA. Images were resolved from imazen/imazen-26's
variant-sets/png-v3-index.tsv by numeric `id`, NOT by filename. Two of the
twenty (1225, 1421) carry transposed dimensions in the gate's cell names —
3000x4000 where the index says 4000x3000 — the known transposed-dimension
defect ACCESS.md records for 196 of 2,160 images. Filename matching misses
exactly those two.
